FROM gemma4:31b-mlx-bf16

# The MLX arm that was supposed to isolate the runtime. gemma4:31b-mlx turned out to be
# nvfp4 -- a 4-bit format -- so it changed precision and runtime at once and told us
# nothing about either in isolation. This tag is the same weights as gemma4:31b-it-bf16
# on a different backend, which is the only way to attribute anything to MLX.
#
# There is a specific reason to bother. Decode on the llama.cpp bf16 model sits at 88%
# of a memory bus that cannot be exceeded if every weight is read once per token, so a
# backend swap should be worth almost nothing. Yet the nvfp4 MLX model measured 178% of
# that same ceiling, with the token count confirmed against wall clock. Either Ollama
# misreports resident size for MLX or the runner is not doing one pass per token. If it
# is the latter, this arm inherits it at full precision and the ceiling argument is
# wrong.
PARAMETER temperature 0.1
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 64
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1
PARAMETER num_predict 24576
PARAMETER stop "<|tool_response>"
PARAMETER stop "<arch_result>"
PARAMETER stop "<tool_result>"
PARAMETER stop "</tool_result>"
